Plans & Plan Review
Plans Review Requirements: The minimum documents and plans information necessary for permit issuance.
Plot Plans: A dimensioned plan view depiction of the project parcel with all existing and proposed elements.
Small Project Plan Review: All residential projects not classified as new residential units.
Site Plan Review Items: Checklist of property details reviewed by Building & Safety for Planning & Development Site Plan approval.
Permits
Building Permit: Required for any project that includes load bearing work or any project exceeding $40K in market value.
Electrical Permit: Required for installing, repairing, or altering electrical wiring or equipment (excluding minor fixture replacements in one/two-family homes).
Mechanical Permit: Required for installing or ugrading heating, air conditioning, and ventilation systems.
Plumbing Permit: Required for new construction, additions, alterations, replacements, all private utilities (Sewer & Water Services), new backflow installs for buildings and irrigation systems. A backflow permit is also required from Durham&apos;s Cross Connection Control Department for any backflow install.
Multi-Trade Permit: Combines multiple trades into a single permit for coordinated projects.
Temporary Power Permit: Allows temporary electrical service for construction or events. Can only be applied if a Building permit is issued.
Stocking Permit: Applies to commercial projects only-for stocking of items used to conduct business prior to issuance of the Certificate of Compliance.
Partial Occupancy Permit: Applies to commercial projects only-for phased occupancy approvals prior to the Certificate of Compliance.
Inspections
Building Inspection Requirements - required inspections for Single Family Residences, Duplexes, and Townhouses.
Who&rsquo;s my inspector today? This link is for Building Inspectors only. For Plumbing, Mechanical, and Electrical, please use the LDO system.
Informal Internal Review (PDF) - Per G.S. 160A-412 and G.S. 153A-352, a form for requesting an informal internal review of inspections decisions is available in our office or online. Please submit completed forms to the Chief or Field Supervisor of that trade. For more information on the internal review process, please call our main number at 919-560-4144.
Online Service Tools
The Land Development Office (LDO) system allows contractors to complete permit and inspection tasks online.
Go here to:
Schedule inspections
Check status of plans review or building permits
Apply for mechanical, plumbing, and electrical permits
Pay fees online
Dplans is a website for digital plan submission. All commercial and residential plan reviews should be submitted through this site.
Go here to:
Submit commercial or residential plans for review
